# History: heat-engine, blind build r01. SPEC 1.0.0 gave this example for REQ-WB-003:
#   `tempC 25, rhPercent 120` ⟶ `T=25.0°C RH=120→100% (rh_clamped) → Tw=25.00°C`
# The formula in REQ-WB-001 gives 25.05. The example had been typed by hand; the blind builder
# followed the formula and recorded the contradiction (r01 choice C-1, then decision D-022). The
# third example had been left unfinished ("Tw=…").
#
# `tilth check` runs every example through the spec's oracle, so the typed value is rejected
# (T002) before any builder sees it. The unfinished one is written `?`: its value is the
# oracle's, shown in the brief and checked by the suite.
tilth 0.1

spec heat-engine-r01 1.0.0
  request {"clock": "2026-05-26T17:00:00.000Z"}

oracle node ../heat-engine/oracle-driver.mjs

op wetBulb
  input tempC number, rhPercent number
  audit text

req WB-003 "Wet-bulb audit summary"
  text
    `result_summary` is `T=<T>°C RH=<rh><markers> → Tw=<Tw>°C`, where `<Tw>` is `wetBulbC`
    fixed to 2 places.
  table wetBulb
    | tempC | rhPercent | audit.result_summary                             |
    | 20    | 50        | "T=20.0°C RH=50% → Tw=13.70°C"                   |
    | 25    | 120       | "T=25.0°C RH=120→100% (rh_clamped) → Tw=25.00°C" |
    | 60    | 2.5       | ?                                                |
